aaeb233a-ea13-42bf-90d7-885434b93f36	vandana.patil@dypiu.ac.in	2025-2026	vc@dypiu.ac.in	vc	178.709090909090917875801096670329570770263671875	297	475.709090909090946297510527074337005615234375	You are suggested to work on the recommendations and suggestions provided by the Dean and the Director of the School	{"acr": [{"vc": "4", "hod": "5", "dean": "4", "label": "Self-motivation and Proactiveness", "director": "4"}, {"vc": "4", "hod": "5", "dean": "4", "label": "Punctuality", "director": "4"}, {"vc": "5", "hod": "4", "dean": "5", "label": "Target based work", "director": "5"}, {"vc": "4", "hod": "4", "dean": "4", "label": "Effectiveness", "director": "4"}, {"vc": "5", "hod": "4", "dean": "5", "label": "Obedience", "director": "5"}], "ict": [{"vc": "5", "hod": "5", "dean": "5", "desc": "Website devloped by usinf Angular", "quad": "III", "type": "ICT Tool -https://shravan250.github.io/vandana-patil/", "score": "5", "title": "Website on Git HUb Published", "director": "5", "quadrant": "III", "description": "Website devloped by usinf Angular"}, {"vc": "5", "hod": "5", "dean": "5", "desc": "To understand complex structure of space and light through laser", "quad": "regular", "type": "pedagogy activity", "score": "5", "title": "Laser simulation in space  video", "director": "5", "quadrant": "regular", "description": "To understand complex structure of space and light through laser"}, {"vc": "5", "hod": "5", "dean": "5", "desc": "to undestand the complex conept", "quad": "regular", "type": "pedagogy activity", "score": "5", "title": "Innovative  pedagoogy", "director": "5", "quadrant": "regular", "description": "to undestand the complex conept"}, {"vc": "5", "hod": "5", "dean": "5", "desc": "This beginner-level course introduces the fundamental physics that underpins modern semiconductor materials and devices. You will start by classifying major types of semiconductors—elemental, compound, organic, amorphous, and nanostructured—and relating their band gaps and carrier mobilities to common applications in integrated circuits, optoelectronics, flexible electronics, and solar cells. The course explains the crystal structures typical of semiconductors, such as diamond and zinc-blende, and shows qualitatively how atomic orbitals combine to form energy bands and band gaps. You will compare direct and indirect band gaps and see how band-gap engineering in semiconductor alloys enables the design of LEDs, lasers, and photovoltaic devices.", "quad": "II", "type": "ICT Tool on coursera", "score": "5", "title": "Coursera course builder for Physics for semiconductor", "director": "5", "quadrant": "II", "description": "This beginner-level course introduces the fundamental physics that underpins modern semiconductor materials and devices. You will start by classifying major types of semiconductors—elemental, compound, organic, amorphous, and nanostructured—and relating their band gaps and carrier mobilities to common applications in integrated circuits, optoelectronics, flexible electronics, and solar cells. The course explains the crystal structures typical of semiconductors, such as diamond and zinc-blende, and shows qualitatively how atomic orbitals combine to form energy bands and band gaps. You will compare direct and indirect band gaps and see how band-gap engineering in semiconductor alloys enables the design of LEDs, lasers, and photovoltaic devices."}, {"vc": "5", "hod": "5", "dean": "5", "desc": "physics courses within Applied Science offers a transformative approach to education. By enabling quick and efficient assessments, it enhances teaching effectiveness and boosts student engagement, while providing valuable data for performance monitoring. The tool allows for personalized learning experiences, helping students grasp complex concepts at their own pace. Additionally, Google Forms is an accessible, cost-effective, and secure platform that simplifies the evaluation process, providing instant feedback that reinforces learning. This real-time feedback helps students identify areas for improvement, deepening their understanding of key semiconductor physics principles. Ultimately, Google Forms not only supports a more interactive and dynamic classroom environment but also empowers students to develop critical analytical and problem-solving skills essential for success in the rapidly evolving field of semiconductor device characterization", "quad": "II", "type": "ICT Tool on coursera", "score": "5", "title": "goole form and myscope tool used", "director": "5", "quadrant": "II", "description": "physics courses within Applied Science offers a transformative approach to education. By enabling quick and efficient assessments, it enhances teaching effectiveness and boosts student engagement, while providing valuable data for performance monitoring. The tool allows for personalized learning experiences, helping students grasp complex concepts at their own pace. Additionally, Google Forms is an accessible, cost-effective, and secure platform that simplifies the evaluation process, providing instant feedback that reinforces learning. This real-time feedback helps students identify areas for improvement, deepening their understanding of key semiconductor physics principles. Ultimately, Google Forms not only supports a more interactive and dynamic classroom environment but also empowers students to develop critical analytical and problem-solving skills essential for success in the rapidly evolving field of semiconductor device characterization"}, {"vc": "5", "hod": "5", "dean": "5", "desc": "ncorporating Google Forms as an ICT tool for conducting quizzes in civil engineering courses within Engineering Physics enhances teaching efficiency, student engagement, and performance monitoring. It enables quick assessment, easy data analysis, and encourages personalized learning, all while being an accessible, cost- effective, and secure platform. This combination of features makes it an ideal tool for modern education i