ACV is a vibrant cultural hub dedicated to preserving and promoting the diverse craft traditions of South Asia. The village hosts over 100 skilled artisans working in dedicated studios, showcasing traditional and contemporary art forms. During the visit, students observed various craft techniques, learned about material processes, and understood the integration of art with marketing and sales strategies. The experience provided valuable real-world insights into artisanship, cultural heritage, and creative entrepreneurship.", "director": "2"}, {"_id": 1779875162262.763, "dean": "5", "name": "Aditya Chari Illustration workshop", "score": 0, "details": "The illustration workshop conducted by Aditya Chari provided students with valuable industry interaction and practical learning experience. Students explored professional illustration techniques, creative processes, digital art practices, and industry trends. The session helped students understand real-world applications of illustration, portfolio development, storytelling, and career opportunities in the creative and design industry through direct interaction with an industry expert.", "director": "2"}], "journals": [{"_id": 1779794344880.94, "dean": "0", "issn": "-", "index": "-", "score": 10, "title": "VIT Ruby Jubilee Celebrations (ICADBSL)", "journal": "International Conference on Innovation in Architecture, design, Buisness, Society, language and literature", "director": "10", "indexing": "-"}, {"_id": 1779887110918.2456, "dean": "0", "issn": "-", "index": "-", "score": 10, "title": "Dnyandarshan 2026", "journal": "National Multidislipanary conference", "director": "20", "indexing": "-"}], "lectures": [{"_id": 1779794344880.5413, "sem": "FYBFA Semester I", "code": "Colour Theory & 2-D Design-IAAR-1005", "dean": "40", "score": 40, "planned": "21", "director": "40", "semester": "FYBFA Semester I", "conducted": "21", "course_code": "Colour Theory & 2-D Design-IAAR-1005", "planned_classes": "21", "conducted_classes": "21"}, {"_id": 1779796784208.9355, "sem": "FYBFA Semester I", "code": "3D Design, AAR-1006", "dean": "40", "score": 40, "planned": "6", "director": "40", "semester": "FYBFA Semester I", "conducted": "6", "course_code": "3D Design, AAR-1006", "planned_classes": "6", "conducted_classes": "6"}, {"_id": 1779796788167.2905, "sem": "FYBFA Semester II", "code": "Semiotics - Semantics-II, AAR-1106", "dean": "40", "score": 40, "planned": "10", "director": "40", "semester": "FYBFA Semester II", "conducted": "10", "course_code": "Semiotics - Semantics-II, AAR-1106", "planned_classes": "10", "conducted_classes": "10"}, {"_id": 1779796791888.8887, "sem": "FYBFA Semester II", "code": "Fundamentals of Layout, AAR-1107", "dean": "40", "score": 40, "planned": "15", "director": "40", "semester": "FYBFA Semester II", "conducted": "15", "course_code": "Fundamentals of Layout, AAR-1107", "planned_classes": "15", "conducted_classes": "15"}], "projects": [{"_id": 1779794344880.7778, "dean": "5", "label": "UG Reaserch Project Guidance", "score": "5", "director": "5"}, {"_id": 1779957828373.0447, "dean": "0", "label": "Other than Curriculum -UmbrelaPainting Competition", "score": "5", "director": "5"}, {"_id": 1779957857309.4468, "dean": "0", "label": "Other than Curriculum - StudentsParticipated in LanternMakingCompetition", "score": "5", "director": "5"}, {"_id": 1779958392262.2695, "dean": "0", "label": "Other than Curriculam - STudents Participoated in YIN Kala Mahostav", "score": "5", "director": "5"}], "research": [{"_id": 1779794344880.1235, "dean": "", "name": "", "score": "", "degree": "", "thesis": "", "student_name": ""}], "training": [{"_id": 1779794344880.2798, "dean": "0", "score": "10", "nature": "Interdisciplinary Collaborative Training", "company": "Dr. D. Y. Patil Institute of Management Studies Students", "director": "10", "duration": "23/03/2026 to 28/03/2026"}], "innovRows": [{"dean": "2", "score": "2", "method": "Used LMS -JUNO ERP", "details": "Regular use of the LMS was carried out for effective academic management and student communication. Attendance was updated regularly on JUNO ERP for maintaining accurate student records. Course content, lecture notes, study materials, assignments, and classroom activity details were uploaded for easy student access. Important academic notices, submissions, and subject-related resources were also shared through the platform. The LMS helped in maintaining organized digital records, smooth communication between teachers and students, and continuous learning support throughout AY 2025–2026.", "director": "2"}, {"dean": "2", "score": "2", "method": "Used Blended learning_Courseera", "details": "The main objective of this blended learning initiative was to encourage students to enhance their knowledge and skills through online learning platforms like Coursera. During AY 2025–2026, every student successfully completed two online courses to gain additional subject knowledge, practical skills, and industry-oriented learning experience. The initiative promoted self-learning, digital learning methods, time management, and continuous skill development beyond classroom teaching. It also helped students improve professional knowledge, creativity, communication, and technical understanding through certified online courses.", "director": "2"}, {"dean": "2", "score": "2", "method": "Project Based Learning- Earth Day", "details": "Under the Fundamentals of Layout subject, students created Earth Day awareness posters to spread environmental and social awareness. The posters were exhibited on campus, and students presented their concepts before jury members, enhancing creativity, presentation skills, and visual communication understanding.", "director": "2"}, {"dean": "2", "score": "2", "method": "Field Visit Learning", "details": "FYBFA students visited Elpro City Square Mall for field-based learning to study wayfinding, space design, branding, semiotics, and semantics through real-life observation, market research, and practical learning experiences beyond the classroom.", "director": "2"}, {"dean": "2", "score": "2", "method": "Educational Tour", "details": "The educational tour to Kerala provided students with learning beyond the classroom through cultural exploration, architectural study, art observation, and experiential learning. The tour enhanced creativity, teamwork, practical knowledge, and real-world understanding", "director": "2"}, {"dean": "0", "score": "0", "method": "Creative Character Design and Game Art Activity for First-Year Students", "details": "The event focused on innovative teaching and learning through interactive games conducted by senior student Anshul. The activity created a fun and engaging learning environment, encouraging teamwork, communication, creative thinking, and active participation while promoting peer learning and collaborative interaction among students. Anshul Mesharma is a final-year student whose work in animation is excellent. He is highly skilled in character design, game design, and storytelling for games. His creative ideas and design process are very inspiring for students. Therefore, I planned an activity with first-year students so they could understand character design, game concepts, and creative storytelling more clearly through interactive learning and guidance from a senior student.", "director": "2"}, {"dean": "0", "score": "0", "method": "Interactive Learning Through Group Discussion and Creative Activities", "details": "The activity encouraged innovative teaching and learning through group discussions, creative thinking, and AI-based techniques. Students explored semiotics, semantics, and wayfinding processes while improving research, teamwork, observation, critical thinking, and presentation skills. AI tools also helped students complete group activities and projects effectively.", "director": "2"}], "proposals": [{"_id": 1779794344880.9631, "dean": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "d