ntic Analysis through Observational Study of Public Behaviour at Elpro City Square Mall", "score": 0, "details": "rand Semiotics and Semantic Analysis through an Observational Study of Public Behaviour during the Visit to Elpro City Square Mall by FYBFA Students: Industry Connect and Learning through Real-World Research Applied in Design Practice", "director": "2"}, {"vc": "0", "_id": 1779853382683.7253, "dean": "0", "name": "Kerala Arts & Crafts Village", "score": 5, "details": "The FYBFA students visited the Kerala Arts & Crafts Village (KACV), located in Vellar near Kovalam, Kerala, as part of their industry exposure programme. Spread across 8.5 acres, KACV is a vibrant cultural hub dedicated to preserving and promoting the diverse craft traditions of South Asia. The village hosts over 100 skilled artisans working in dedicated studios, showcasing traditional and contemporary art forms. During the visit, students observed various craft techniques, learned about material processes, and understood the integration of art with marketing and sales strategies. The experience provided valuable real-world insights into artisanship, cultural heritage, and creative entrepreneurship.", "director": "2"}, {"vc": "5", "_id": 1779875162262.763, "dean": "5", "name": "Aditya Chari Illustration workshop", "score": 0, "details": "The illustration workshop conducted by Aditya Chari provided students with valuable industry interaction and practical learning experience. Students explored professional illustration techniques, creative processes, digital art practices, and industry trends. The session helped students understand real-world applications of illustration, portfolio development, storytelling, and career opportunities in the creative and design industry through direct interaction with an industry expert.", "director": "2"}], "journals": [{"vc": "0", "_id": 1779794344880.94, "dean": "0", "issn": "-", "index": "-", "score": 10, "title": "VIT Ruby Jubilee Celebrations (ICADBSL)",