 Academy Educator", "score": "5", "director": "5"}], "awards": [{"hod": "", "date": "", "level": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "director": "", "award_date": ""}], "patents": [{"hod": "", "date": "26/09/2026", "type": "National", "score": "40", "title": "A Device for Mental welbeing", "fileNo": "202521092414", "status": "Provisional", "file_no": "202521092414", "director": "30", "patent_date": "26/09/2026", "patent_status": "Provisional"}], "society": [{"hod": "", "label": "", "score": "", "details": "", "activity": "", "director": ""}], "uniActs": [{"hod": "", "score": "5", "nature": "Established and coordinated the AWS Cloud Club as a student-driven technical initiative to promote awareness, practical learning, innovation, and industry-oriented skill development in Cloud Computing, DevOps, and emerging technologies. The club activities focused on hands-on workshops, peer learning, technical discussions, certification awareness, cloud project development, hackathons, expert sessions, and industry interaction to enhance students’ technical competencies and employability skills.", "activity": "AWS Cloud Club Formation", "director": "5"}, {"score": "15", "nature": "Coordinated and facilitated the CSR-funded AWS Cloud Automation & DevOps (CAD) Program under the AWS re/Start initiative aimed at empowering students with industry-relevant cloud computing and DevOps skills. The program focused on hands-on training, practical implementation, career readiness, certification preparation, soft skills development, and employability enhancement through real-world cloud and automation practices aligned with current IT industry standards. Successfully contributed to program execution, student engagement, and institutional collaboration, generating a revenue of approximately ₹1.38 Lakhs through training and academic initiatives.", "activity": "CSR Funded AWS CAD Program (AWS reStart)", "director": "15"}, {"score": "5", "nature": "Dicipline Committee", "activity": "Convocation  2026", "director": "3"}, {"score": "5", "nature": "Lunch Committee", "activity": "Diksharamb Program 2025", "director": "5"}], "deptActs": [{"hod": "", "score": "5", "nature": "Cordinator NAAC 3 Criteria", "activity": "NAAC", "director": "3"}, {"score": "10", "nature": "BCA TY Project", "activity": "Project Coordinator", "director": "5"}, {"score": "5", "nature": "Btech CSE", "activity": "Project Guide", "director": "3"}], "feedback": [{"fb1": "91.14", "fb2": "91.14", "hod": "", "code": "CSA3102- Cloud Automation and DevOps Sem 6", "score": "9.1", "director": "9", "feedback_1": "91.14", "feedback_2": "91.14", "course_code": "CSA3102- Cloud Automation and DevOps Sem 6"}, {"fb1": "93.05", "fb2": "93.05", "code": "CLC3101- Cloud Infrastructure Orchestration Sem 6", "score": "9.3", "director": "9", "feedback_1": "93.05", "feedback_2": "93.05", "course_code": "CLC3101- Cloud Infrastructure Orchestration Sem 6"}], "industry": [{"hod": "", "name": "DevOps Training Delivery at Bitwise Inc.", "score": "5", "details": "Delivered industry-oriented DevOps training sessions at Bitwise Inc. focusing on practical implementation of CI/CD pipelines, Linux administration, Git, Jenkins, Docker, Kubernetes, cloud deployment, automation tools, and DevOps best practices. The training emphasized hands-on learning, real-time industry scenarios, troubleshooting techniques, and workflow automation to enhance participants’ technical competency and industry readiness.", "director": "5"}, {"name": "MoU Collaboration with ILEMTEC for AWS re/Start Program", "score": "5", "details": "Facilitated and contributed to the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) collaboration between the institution and ILEMTEC for the successful implementation of the AWS re/Start Program. The collaboration aimed to strengthen industry-academia engagement by providing students with hands-on training, cloud computing and DevOps skill development, career readiness support, certification awareness, and enhanced employa