ions by operating entirely within the browser. The platform utilizes a custom Runge-Kutta (RK4) physics engine to dynamically solve and visualize complex kinematics for Single-Degree-of-Freedom (SDOF), vehicle suspension, and rotor balancing systems. By allowing users to actively manipulate variables such as mass, stiffness, and damping, the tool provides instant feedback on mechanical responses across various operational regimes. Furthermore, advanced visual analytics translate abstract mathematics into real-time mechanical animations, interactive phase plots, and transmissibility curves using dynamic browser rendering. Ultimately, the simulator bridges theoretical concepts and practical application, empowering students to conduct virtual experiments and export raw CSV data for empirical lab reporting.", "quad": "Quadrant III", "type": "Web App", "score": "5", "title": "Noise VIbration and Harshness Simulator", "director": "5", "quadrant": "Quadrant III", "description": "Vibrations Lab Pro is an interactive, web-based NVH simulator that eliminates the need for software installations by operating entirely within the browser. The platform utilizes a custom Runge-Kutta (RK4) physics engine to dynamically solve and visualize complex kinematics for Single-Degree-of-Freedom (SDOF), vehicle suspension, and rotor balancing systems. By allowing users to actively manipulate variables such as mass, stiffness, and damping, the tool provides instant feedback on mechanical responses across various operational regimes. Furthermore, advanced visual analytics translate abstract mathematics into real-time mechanical animations, interactive phase plots, and transmissibility curves using dynamic browser rendering. Ultimately, the simulator bridges theoretical concepts and practical application, empowering students to conduct virtual experiments and export raw CSV data for empirical lab reporting."}, {"desc": "A student-focused website offering easy access to course materials and a blo