1c46cd47-6f70-44df-aaa0-2b0bc7bf145d	vandana.patil@dypiu.ac.in	2025-2026	anupama.patil@dypiu.ac.in	director	178.709090909090917875801096670329570770263671875	297	475.709090909090946297510527074337005615234375	Dr. Vandana Patil has an outstanding academic record, receives good student feedback, and she is a wonderful researcher with high-quality publications.  She does a good job in mentoring first-year students for innovative projects, encouraging them to participate in hackathons, and connecting them with top research labs like NCL and DRDO. It is suggested that, she needs to step up as a team player and take more personal initiative in department and school-level activities. She should also focus her efforts on bringing in outside research grants (extramural funding) and securing consultancy projects from different industries.	{"acr": [{"hod": "5", "label": "Self-motivation and Proactiveness", "director": "4"}, {"hod": "5", "label": "Punctuality", "director": "4"}, {"hod": "4", "label": "Target based work", "director": "5"}, {"hod": "4", "label": "Effectiveness", "director": "4"}, {"hod": "4", "label": "Obedience", "director": "5"}], "ict": [{"hod": "5", "desc": "Website devloped by usinf Angular", "quad": "III", "type": "ICT Tool -https://shravan250.github.io/vandana-patil/", "score": "5", "title": "Website on Git HUb Published", "director": "5", "quadrant": "III", "description": "Website devloped by usinf Angular"}, {"hod": "5", "desc": "To understand complex structure of space and light through laser", "quad": "regular", "type": "pedagogy activity", "score": "5", "title": "Laser simulation in space  video", "director": "5", "quadrant": "regular", "description": "To understand complex structure of space and light through laser"}, {"hod": "5", "desc": "to undestand the complex conept", "quad": "regular", "type": "pedagogy activity", "score": "5", "title": "Innovative  pedagoogy", "director": "5", "quadrant": "regular", "description": "to undestand the complex conept"}, {"hod": "5", "desc": "This beginner-level course introduces the fundamental physics that underpins modern semiconductor materials and devices. You will start by classifying major types of semiconductors—elemental, compound, organic, amorphous, and nanostructured—and relating their band gaps and carrier mobilities to common applications in integrated circuits, optoelectronics, flexible electronics, and solar cells. The course explains the crystal structures typical of semiconductors, such as diamond and zinc-blende, and shows qualitatively how atomic orbitals combine to form energy bands and band gaps. You will compare direct and indirect band gaps and see how band-gap engineering in semiconductor alloys enables the design of LEDs, lasers, and photovoltaic devices.", "quad": "II", "type": "ICT Tool on coursera", "score": "5", "title": "Coursera course builder for Physics for semiconductor", "director": "5", "quadrant": "II", "description": "This beginner-level course introduces the fundamental physics that underpins modern semiconductor materials and devices. You will start by classifying major types of semiconductors—elemental, compound, organic, amorphous, and nanostructured—and relating their band gaps and carrier mobilities to common applications in integrated circuits, optoelectronics, flexible electronics, and solar cells. The course explains the crystal structures typical of semiconductors, such as diamond and zinc-blende, and shows qualitatively how atomic orbitals combine to form energy bands and band gaps. You will compare direct and indirect band gaps and see how band-gap engineering in semiconductor alloys enables the design of LEDs, lasers, and photovoltaic devices."}, {"hod": "5", "desc": "physics courses within Applied Science offers a transformative approach to education. By enabling quick and efficient assessments, it enhances teaching effectiveness and boosts student engagement, while providing valuable data for performance monitoring. The tool allows for personalized learning experiences, helping students grasp complex concepts at their own pace. Additionally, Google Forms is an accessible, cost-effective, and secure platform that simplifies the evaluation process, providing instant feedback that reinforces learning. This real-time feedback helps students identify areas for improvement, deepening their understanding of key semiconductor physics principles. Ultimately, Google Forms not only supports a more interactive and dynamic classroom environment but also empowers students to develop critical analytical and problem-solving skills essential for success in the rapidly evolving field of semiconductor device characterization", "quad": "II", "type": "ICT Tool on coursera", "score": "5", "title": "goole form and myscope tool used", "director": "5", "quadrant": "II", "description": "physics courses within Applied Science offers a transformative approach to education. By enabling quick and efficient assessments, it enhances teaching effectiveness and boosts student engagement, while providing valuable data for performance monitoring. The tool allows for personalized learning experiences, helping students grasp complex concepts at their own pace. Additionally, Google Forms is an accessible, cost-effective, and secure platform that simplifies the evaluation process, providing instant feedback that reinforces learning. This real-time feedback helps students identify areas for improvement, deepening their understanding of key semiconductor physics principles. Ultimately, Google Forms not only supports a more interactive and dynamic classroom environment but also empowers students to develop critical analytical and problem-solving skills essential for success in the rapidly evolving field of semiconductor device characterization"}, {"hod": "5", "desc": "ncorporating Google Forms as an ICT tool for conducting quizzes in civil engineering courses within Engineering Physics enhances teaching efficiency, student engagement, and performance monitoring. It enables quick assessment, easy data analysis, and encourages personalized learning, all while being an accessible, cost- effective, and secure platform. This combination of features makes it an ideal tool for modern education in technical fields like civil engineering. This platform also helps to streamline the assessment process, and provide instant feedback that helps them improve their understanding of key concepts", "quad": "II", "type": "Google classroom", "score": "5", "title": "Google classroom", "director": "5", "quadrant": "II", "description": "ncorporating Google Forms as an ICT tool for conducting quizzes in civil engineering courses within Engineering Physics enhances teaching efficiency, student engagement, and performance monitoring. It enables quick assessment, easy data analysis, and encourages personalized learning, all while being an accessible, cost- effective, and secure platform. This combination of features makes it an ideal tool for modern education in technical fields like civil engineering. This platform also helps to streamline the assessment process, and provide instant feedback that helps them improve their understanding of key concepts"}], "fdps": [{"hod": "5", "org": "AICTE ATAL acdemy Govt of India Nelson Mandela Marg, Vasant Kunj, New Delhi -110070", "score": "5", "program": "Faculty Development Program on Secure and Explainable Generative AI  for Medical IoT Data Analytics at National Institute of Technology Puducherry from", "director": "5", "duration": "25/08/2025 to 30/08/2025", "organization": "AICTE ATAL acdemy Govt of India Nelson Mandela Marg, Vasant Kunj, New Delhi -110070"}, {"hod": "5", "org": "AICTE ATAL acdemy Govt of India Nelson Mandela Marg, Vasant Kunj, New Delhi -110070", "score": "5", "program": "Academy Faculty Development Program on Security and Privacy issues and their countermeasures in the era of Artificial Intelligence at DELHI TECHNOLOGICAL UNIVERSITY from .", "directo