own pace and become a skilled CAD designer and simulation engineer."}, {"type": "Web App", "score": "5", "title": "Noise VIbration and Harshness Simulator", "quadrant": "Quadrant III", "description": "Vibrations Lab Pro is an interactive, web-based NVH simulator that eliminates the need for software installations by operating entirely within the browser. The platform utilizes a custom Runge-Kutta (RK4) physics engine to dynamically solve and visualize complex kinematics for Single-Degree-of-Freedom (SDOF), vehicle suspension, and rotor balancing systems. By allowing users to actively manipulate variables such as mass, stiffness, and damping, the tool provides instant feedback on mechanical responses across various operational regimes. Furthermore, advanced visual analytics translate abstract mathematics into real-time mechanical animations, interactive phase plots, and transmissibility curves using dynamic browser rendering. Ultimately, the simulator bridges theoretical concepts and practical application, empowering students to conduct virtual experiments and export raw CSV data for empirical lab reporting."}, {"type": "Website (https://thedineshkumar.com)", "score": "5", "title": "Public Website with Blog and Course Content", "quadrant": "Quadrant III", "description": "A student-focused website offering easy access to course materials and a blog highlighting the latest research breakthroughs in mechanical engineering. The website Includes Video Lectures, PPT lectures,PDF Notes, Blog."}, {"type": "Coursera", "score": "5", "title": "Course Builder", "quadrant": "Quadrant I,II", "description": "Design of Machine Elements Coursera Builder Course"}], "ipr": [], "fdps": [{"hod": "", "score": "10", "program": "Outcome based Education", "director": "", "duration": "22-26 May 2025", "organization": "DYPIU"}, {"score": "10", "program": "Emerging Technologies in Industry 4.0 and 5.0", "duration": "15-19 Aug 2025", "organization": "DYPIU"}, {"score": "10", "program": "Five-Day