dmission outreach activities during admission campaign visits at Patna for student interaction and programme awareness.", "activity": "Admission Activities and Programme Coordination"}, {"score": "30", "nature": "Nominated as a member of the University Doctoral Committee for framing guidelines, reviewing academic and research-related matters, and supporting the conduct of Ph.D. and Postdoctoral programmes in interdisciplinary research domains. Contributed to discussions related to research governance, doctoral programme development, academic policies, and research activities at the university level.", "activity": "Doctoral Committee Member"}, {"score": "10", "nature": "Coordinated food management activities during the University Foundation Day celebration, including planning, arrangement, distribution, and monitoring of food services for participants, guests, faculty members, staff, and students. Ensured smooth coordination with organizing teams and vendors for effective execution of hospitality and event support activities.", "activity": "Foundation Day Celebration – Food Management"}, {"score": "10", "nature": "Served as a member of the Discipline Committee for Indus Fiesta and coordinated discipline, crowd management, participant movement, and venue monitoring activities. Ensured adherence to event guidelines, maintained orderly conduct during programme activities, and coordinated with organizing teams for smooth execution of the university-level event.", "activity": "Indus Fiesta – Discipline Committee"}, {"score": "10", "nature": "Served as a member of the Seating Arrangement and Discipline Team during the University Convocation. Coordinated seating arrangements for graduates, parents, dignitaries, faculty members, and guests in accordance with the approved convocation programme flow. Oversaw venue discipline, participant movement, seating allocation, and crowd management to ensure smooth execution of convocation proceedings and adherence to the event schedule.", "activity": "Convocation – Seating Arrangement and Discipline"}], "deptActs": [{"hod": "", "score": "10", "nature": "Served as Criteria 7 Incharge at School Level for preparation, coordination, compilation, verification, and maintenance of NAAC-related documentation, reports, data collection, evidence management, and quality assurance activities.", "activity": "NAAC Criteria 7 School Level Documentation", "director": ""}, {"score": "10", "nature": "Led programme booklet preparation and syllabus coordination activities for B.Tech. (CSE), BCA, MCA, and M.Sc. (Computational Mathematics) programmes for current and upcoming academic years. Designed standardized LaTeX syllabus templates, guided and trained faculty members for LaTeX-based syllabus preparation, coordinated follow-ups for syllabus submission and corrections, verified and consolidated academic documents, and compiled programme-wise booklet documentation for academic circulation and record maintenance.", "activity": "Programme Booklet and Syllabus Coordination"}, {"score": "5", "nature": "Coordinated and monitored academic and administrative activities for First Year Div C and Div D during Semester II including student and parent communication, follow-ups regarding pending fees, JUNO updates, feedback forms, Coursera Ethics course completion, academic reminders, mentoring support, faculty coordination, syllabus update follow-ups, course file documentation activities, and smooth execution of academic processes.", "activity": "FY Academic In-charge – Div C and Div D (Sem-II)"}, {"score": "3", "nature": "Coordinated seating arrangement activities during the Student Induction Program, leading the team responsible for planning, organizing, and managing seating arrangements for newly admitted students and parents. Ensured smooth venue management, participant guidance, crowd coordination, and orderly conduct of the induction programme.", "activity": "Induction Program"}], "feedback": [{"hod": "", "score": "7.5", "