unities through guidance, motivation, and business development support. Contributed towards promoting women empowerment, self-employment, and sustainable community development initiatives.", "activity": "Social Outreach & Women Entrepreneurship Development", "director": ""}, {"score": "5", "details": "Actively connected with NGOs and social organizations through the Rural Internship initiative to provide students with community exposure and social learning experiences.", "activity": "Social Outreach & Community Engagement"}], "uniActs": [{"hod": "", "score": "10", "nature": "actively contributed towards promoting innovation, entrepreneurship, and student engagement activities at the university level. Coordinated and supported various academic, innovation, startup, and skill-development initiatives conducted under the IIC framework.  Key contributions included:  Planning and organizing IIC activities, workshops, expert sessions, and innovation-related events Promoting entrepreneurship, startup culture, and innovation awareness among students Coordinating student participation in innovation and incubation initiatives Collaborating with faculty members, industry experts, and institutional departments for smooth execution of activities Supporting documentation, reporting, and submission of IIC annual activities and achievements Encouraging experiential learning, problem-solving, and creative thinking among students Contributing towards strengthening the university’s innovation and entrepreneurial ecosystem", "activity": "Served as President – Institution’s Innovation Council (IIC)", "director": ""}, {"score": "10", "nature": "Served as the University Level Coordinator for Smart India Hackathon (SIH) 2025 and actively coordinated student participation, communication, and event-related activities for the national innovation initiative.", "activity": "University Level Responsibility – Smart India Hackathon (SIH) 2025 Coordinator"}, {"score": "10", "nature": "Served as the University Internship In-Charge and provided centralized coordination and support for internship-related activities across all schools/departments of the university.Developed University level Internship Policy", "activity": "University Level Responsibility – Internship In-Charge"}, {"score": "10", "nature": "In-Charge of Centre for Innovation, Incubation and Entrepreneurship (CIIE) and actively contributed towards promoting innovation, entrepreneurship, startup culture, and incubation activities within the university ecosystem.", "activity": "In-Charge CIIE"}], "deptActs": [{"hod": "", "score": "10", "nature": "as Internship In-Charge for the department and University handled end-to-end coordination and assistance for students with respect to Rural Internships and Industrial Internships. Facilitated the complete internship process including student guidance, communication, documentation, industry coordination, monitoring, and report submission activities.", "activity": "Internship Coordination & Student Support", "director": ""}, {"score": "10", "nature": "Actively contributed to departmental activities by assisting in the organization and coordination of guest lectures, expert sessions, and student development activities.", "activity": "Academic & Event Support"}], "feedback": [{"hod": "", "score": "8.0", "director": "", "feedback_1": "80.25", "feedback_2": "80.25", "course_code": "MF1002/Management Fundamentals"}], "industry": [{"hod": "", "name": "Ray of Hope", "score": "2", "details": "Coordinated Rural Internship collaboration and community engagement activities through institutional association with Ray of Hope and signed MoU", "director": ""}, {"name": "Prayaas Youth Foundation", "score": "2", "details": "Established collaboration for Rural Internship activities to provide students with practical exposure to rural development, NGO functioning, and community-based learning. Supported student engagement in social impact and field-based experiential learning programs and signed Mou"}, {"name": "Wings for Dream", "score": "2", "details": "Facilitated NGO partnership and Rural Internship opportunities for students through experiential and community-oriented learning initiatives. Contributed towards enhancing student awareness regarding social development, teamwork, and field engagement activities. signe MoU"}], "journals": [{"hod": "", "issn": "", "score": "", "title": "", "journal": "", "director": "", "indexing": ""}], "lectures": [{"hod": "", "score": "50", "director": "", "semester": "Sem 1", "course_code": "MF1002", "planned_classes": "20", "conducted_classes": "21"}], "products": [{"hod": "", "score": "", "usage": "", "details": "", "director": ""}], "projects": [{"hod": "", "label": "", "score": "", "director": ""}], "research": [{"hod": "", "score": "", "degree": "", "thesis": "", "director": "", "student_name": ""}], "training": [{"hod": "", "score": "", "nature": "", "company": "", "director": "", "duration": ""}], "innovRows": [{"score": "2", "method": "Activity-Based / Experiential Learning Technique", "details": "Designed and implemented an application-oriented assignment on “Administration vs Management in Different Organisations and Situations” integrating the 5 Functions of Management (Planning, Organizing, Staffing, Directing, and Controlling). Students prepared organizational charts, flowcharts, and practical business components such as KPIs, SOPs, mini budgets, and training checklists to connect theoretical concepts with real-world organizational practices."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Presentation-Based / Collaborative Learning Technique", "details": "Conducted group presentation activities for BBA students under the subject Management Fundamentals to promote collaborative and participative learning. Students were divided into groups and assigned various management topics such as Planning, Organizing, Staffing, Leadership, Communication, Motivation, and Controlling."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Quiz-Based / ERP-Enabled Interactive Assessment Technique", "details": "Conducted MCQ-based quizzes through the ERP platform as part of continuous assessment in Management Fundamentals to promote technology-enabled learning and student engagement. The quiz covered topics such as the Nature, Importance, Functions, and Evolution of Management through structured objective-based evaluation."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Experiential Learning through Event Participation / SIH 2025 Volunteer Engagement", "details": "This initiative helped students:  Understand the practical application of management functions Develop teamwok, leadership, and interpersonral skills"}, {"score": "2", "method": "Industry Interaction / Professional Development Learning Technique", "details": "Organized an expert session by Chetan Khairnar,Sr.Manager Corporate Relations  to provide students with practical insights into professional behavior, corporate culture, and industry expectations."}], "projects2": [{"hod": "", "role": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "sanction_date": "", "project_status": ""}], "proposals": [{"hod": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "director": "", "duration": ""}], "courseFile": [{"hod": "", "score": "20", "title": "BBA/SEM I", "course": "Management Fundamentals", "details": "1.Available", "director": ""}], "innovScore": "10", "innovDetails": "Activity-Based / Experiential Learning Technique, Presentation-Based / Collaborative Learning Technique, Quiz-Based / ERP-Enabled Interactive Assessment Technique, Experiential Learning through Event Participation / SIH 2025 Volunteer Engagement, Industry Interaction / Professional Development Learning Technique", "externalProjects": [{"hod": "", "role": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "sanction_date": "", "project_status": ""}], "internalProjects": [], "summaryOtherInfo": "Key Contributions & Institutional Impact\\n\\n1. President - Institution’s Innovation Council (IIC):\\n\\nAs President of the Institution’s Innovation Council (IIC), successfully established and strengthened the university’s innovation ecosystem in alignment with the guidelines of the Ministry of Education’s Innovation Cell (MIC). Led the effective implementation of the IIC calendar through innovation, startup, entrepreneurship, IPR, design thinking, research, and skill-development initiatives. Under my leadership and continuous mentoring, students actively participated and secured achievements at state-level and national-level innovation, entrepreneurship, startup, and hackathon platforms, significantly enhancing the university’s innovation culture, institutional visibility, and external recognition.\\n\\n2. In-Charge -CIIE :\\n\\nPlayed a foundational role in establishing, operationalizing, and strengthening the Centre for Innovation, Incubation & Entrepreneurship (CIIE) at DYPIU. Contributed extensively towards strategic planning, policy development, startup ecosystem building, programme execution, institutional networking, operational management, and entrepreneurship development initiatives. Successfully coordinated startup mentoring, incubation and pre-incubation programmes, innovation challenges, workshops, Faculty Development Programmes (FDPs), expert sessions, industry interactions, and entrepreneurship awareness activities.\\n\\nAlso played a significant role in the establishment and coordination of Dnyanavishkar Foundation, a Section 8 Company, contributing towards entrepreneurship promotion, innovation-driven initiatives, social impact activities, and ecosystem development aligned with institutional and societal objectives.\\n\\nThrough dedicated efforts, consistent coordination, and ecosystem development initiatives, the department achieved significant growth and received national-level recognition, entrepreneurship excellence awards, appreciation, and institutional acknowledgements, thereby strengthening DYPIU’s position in innovation and entrepreneurship development.\\n\\n3. Internship In-Charge (Coordination, Industry Connect & Social Outreach):\\n\\nSuccessfully managed and coordinated university-level internship activities by facilitating industry interactions, student mentoring, documentation, execution, and monitoring processes across programmes. Strengthened industry-academia collaboration by connecting students with industries, startups, organizations, NGOs, and sector experts for experiential and skill-based learning opportunities.\\n\\nInitiated collaborations and MoUs with NGOs and social organizations for Rural Internship and social outreach initiatives to promote community engagement, social responsibility, experiential learning, and rural exposure among students. Contributed towards impactful outreach activities aligned with institutional values and Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).\\n\\n4. Student Achievement, Teaching Excellence & Institutional Contribution:\\n\\nUnder my guidance, mentoring support, and departmental leadership, students actively participated and achieved recognition in several state-level and national-level innovation, entrepreneurship, startup, and competition platforms. Through continuous ecosystem development and programme execution, DYPIU received multiple recognitions, appreciation certificates, entrepreneurship excellence awards, and institutional acknowledgements in the areas of innovation, incubation, entrepreneurship, and student development.\\n\\nAlongside administrative and innovation responsibilities, serving as a Faculty member in Management Studies for first-year BBA students by delivering Fundamentals of Management through innovative, practical, and industry-oriented teaching methodologies. Integrating experiential learning, case studies, discussions, critical thinking, and real-world applications to enhance conceptual clarity, leadership mindset, communication skills, and overall student development.\\n\\n5. Academic, Administrative & Institutional Responsibility:\\n\\nActively contributed to the planning, coordination, management, and successful execution of university-level academic, administrative, institutional development, student engagement, innovation, entrepreneurship, and outreach activities. Demonstrated strong leadership, multitasking, coordination, and organizational abilities by efficiently handling multiple responsibilities beyond regular academic duties. Played a vital role in supporting university administration in the smooth execution of institutional programmes, strategic initiatives, events, collaborations, and student-centric activities while ensuring operational excellence and effective implementation.\\n\\nDemonstrated exceptional commitment, ownership, accountability, and dedication by consistently contributing extended efforts and additional working hours towards the successful establishment and execution of Internship Coordination, IIC, CIIE, innovation initiatives, student-centric programmes, institutional activities, and university development goals entrusted by the administration.", "sectionSaveStatus": {"partA": true, "partB": true}, "sectionApplicability": {"society": "applicable", "projects": "notApplicable", "research": "notApplicable"}}, "status": "Pending Director Review", "totals": {"grandTotal": 263.025, "partATotal": 163.025, "partBTotal": 100, "effectiveGrandMax": 510, "effectivePartAMax": 165, "effectivePartBMax": 345}, "review_chain": ["director", "dean", "vc"], "academic_year": "2025-2026", "next_reviewer": "director", "workflow_status": "Pending Director Review", "submitter_profile": {"email": "sandhya.ingale@dypiu.ac.in", "school": "SoCM", "full_name": "Dr. Sandhya Ingale", "department": "", "experience": "14.5", "designation": "Assistant Professor", "employee_id": "20181011", "qualification": "MBA,M.Phil, DLL&LW, Ph.D", "appraisal_role": "faculty", "reportsToRegistrar": false, "teaching_experience": "14.5", "reports_to_registrar": false}, "next_reviewer_role": "director"}	