7ecf45a42553796b866ae6563_case_study_(1)_compressed.pdf"}], "innov-4": [{"url": "/api/v1/upload/view/faculty-appraisal/innov-4/7548edcc4107e62b82c4956605556045bb2f5cc126449540cc27883c620c721c_lab_manual_cad_%281%29_compressed.pdf", "name": "lab manual cad (1)_compressed.pdf", "type": "application/pdf", "publicId": "faculty-appraisal/innov-4/7548edcc4107e62b82c4956605556045bb2f5cc126449540cc27883c620c721c_lab_manual_cad_(1)_compressed.pdf"}], "train-0": [{"url": "/api/v1/upload/view/faculty-appraisal/train-0/0670f8cd5e76f14e67d3f236a2c930868fff94f67716af93a4017cebda002561_Invitation_as_Corporate_Training.pdf", "name": "Invitation as Corporate Training.pdf", "type": "application/pdf", "publicId": "faculty-appraisal/train-0/0670f8cd5e76f14e67d3f236a2c930868fff94f67716af93a4017cebda002561_Invitation_as_Corporate_Training.pdf"}]}, "form": {"acr": [{"label": "Self-motivation and Proactiveness"}, {"label": "Punctuality"}, {"label": "Target based work"}, {"label": "Effectiveness"}, {"label": "Obedience"}], "ict": [{"hod": "", "type": "Innovative Teaching-Learning Methodology", "score": "10", "title": "Technology-Enabled Experiential Learning using Cloud Platforms", "director": "", "quadrant": "Quadrant II – E-Content (Video, Demonstration & Practical Learning Resources)", "description": "Live demonstrations of cloud services and DevOps tools. Industry-oriented mini-projects and capstone projects."}, {"type": "E content", "score": "10", "title": "own youtube channel", "quadrant": "Quadrant II – E-Content", "description": "https://youtube.com/@professorfactory?si=fW3VFIAGCQiyv06n"}], "ipr": [], "fdps": [{"hod": "", "score": "", "program": "", "director": "", "duration": "", "organization": ""}], "info": {"ay": "2025-2026", "name": "Dr Swapnil Waghmare", "qual": "", "desig": "Assistant Professor", "expDyp": "", "school": "SoCSEA", "expPrev": "", "expTotal": "", "experience": ""}, "books": [{"hod": "", "book": "", "issn": "", "score": "", "title": "", "coauthor": "", "director": "", "publisher": "", "first_author": ""}], "confs": [{"hod": "", "type": "Resource Person", "level": "UG", "score": "10", "title": "Invitation as a Resource Person for a workshop on AWS Security at SSPU, Kiwale", "director": "", "organization": "SSPU, Kiwale, Pune"}], "quals": [{"hod": "", "label": "AWS Solution Architect Certified", "score": "5", "director": ""}, {"label": "AWS Academy Educator", "score": "5"}], "awards": [{"hod": "", "level": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "director": "", "award_date": ""}], "patents": [{"hod": "", "type": "National", "score": "40", "title": "A Device for Mental welbeing", "file_no": "202521092414", "director": "", "patent_date": "26/09/2026", "patent_status": "Provisional"}], "society": [{"hod": "", "score": "", "details": "", "activity": "", "director": ""}], "uniActs": [{"hod": "", "score": "5", "nature": "Established and coordinated the AWS Cloud Club as a student-driven technical initiative to promote awareness, practical learning, innovation, and industry-oriented skill development in Cloud Computing, DevOps, and emerging technologies. The club activities focused on hands-on workshops, peer learning, technical discussions, certification awareness, cloud project development, hackathons, expert sessions, and industry interaction to enhance students’ technical competencies and employability skills.", "activity": "AWS Cloud Club Formation", "director": ""}, {"score": "15", "nature": "Coordinated and facilitated the CSR-funded AWS Cloud Automation & DevOps (CAD) Program under the AWS re/Start initiative aimed at empowering students with industry-relevant cloud computing and DevOps skills. The program focused on hands-on training, practical implementation, career readiness, certification preparation, soft skills development, and employability enhancement through real-world cloud and automation practices aligned with current IT industry standards. Successfully contributed to program execution, student engagement, and institutional collaboration, generating a revenue of approximately ₹1.38 Lakhs through training and academic initiatives.", "activity": "CSR Funded AWS CAD Program (AWS reStart)"}, {"score": "5", "nature": "Dicipline Committee", "activity": "Convocation  2026"}, {"score": "5", "nature": "Lunch Committee", "activity": "Diksharamb Program 2025"}], "deptActs": [{"hod": "", "score": "5", "nature": "Cordinator NAAC 3 Criteria", "activity": "NAAC", "director": ""}, {"score": "10", "nature": "BCA TY Project", "activity": "Project Coordinator"}, {"score": "5", "nature": "Btech CSE", "activity": "Project Guide"}], "feedback": [{"hod": "", "score": "9.1", "director": "", "feedback_1": "91.14", "feedback_2": "91.14", "course_code": "CSA3102- Cloud Automation and DevOps Sem 6"}, {"score": "9.3", "feedback_1": "93.05", "feedback_2": "93.05", "course_code": "CLC3101- Cloud Infrastructure Orchestration Sem 6"}], "industry": [{"hod": "", "name": "DevOps Training Delivery at Bitwise Inc.", "score": "5", "details": "Delivered industry-oriented DevOps training sessions at Bitwise Inc. focusing on practical implementation of CI/CD pipelines, Linux administration, Git, Jenkins, Docker, Kubernetes, cloud deployment, automation tools, and DevOps best practices. The training emphasized hands-on learning, real-time industry scenarios, troubleshooting techniques, and workflow automation to enhance participants’ technical competency and industry readiness.", "director": ""}, {"name": "MoU Collaboration with ILEMTEC for AWS re/Start Program", "score": "5", "details": "Facilitated and contributed to the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) collaboration between the institution and ILEMTEC for the successful implementation of the AWS re/Start Program. The collaboration aimed to strengthen industry-academia engagement by providing students with hands-on training, cloud computing and DevOps skill development, career readiness support, certification awareness, and enhanced employability opportunities aligned with current IT industry requirements."}], "journals": [{"hod": "", "issn": "1005-0930", "score": "30", "title": "Health Monitoring System Integrating IoT and Machine Learning for Cardiac Prognosis", "journal": "Journal of Basic Science and Engineering", "director": "", "indexing": "Scopus"}, {"issn": "OI: 10.1109/INCSST64791.2025.11210339", "score": "30", "title": "Crop Recommendation Using Comparative Machine Learning Techniques with a Tuned CatBoost Classifier", "journal": "International Conference on Smart & Sustainable Technology", "indexing": "Scopus"}, {"issn": "979-8-3503-9177-0", "score": "30", "title": "IoT-Enabled Heart Disease Prediction: Harnessing Machine Learning for Proactive Healthcare", "journal": "International Conference on Computing, Communication, Control and Automation (ICCUBEA)", "indexing": "Scopus"}], "lectures": [{"hod": "", "score": "10", "director": "", "semester": "V", "course_code": "CSA3004 Cloud Native Orchestration", "planned_classes": "40", "conducted_classes": "38"}, {"hod": "", "score": "10", "director": "", "semester": "V", "course_code": "CLC3001 Fundamental of Cloud Computing", "planned_classes": "35", "conducted_classes": "35"}, {"hod": "", "score": "10", "director": "", "semester": "VI", "course_code": "CSA3102 Cloud Automation and Devops", "planned_classes": "35", "conducted_classes": "35"}, {"hod": "", "score": "10", "director": "", "semester": "VI", "course_code": "CLC3101 Cloud Infrastructure Orchestration", "planned_classes": "35", "conducted_classes": "35"}, {"hod": "", "score": "10", "director": "", "semester": "VI", "course_code": "CSA3106 Capstone Project", "planned_classes": "35", "conducted_classes": "35"}], "products": [{"hod": "", "score": "", "usage": "", "details": "", "director": ""}], "projects": [{"hod": "", "label": "", "score": "", "director": ""}], "research": [{"hod": "", "score": "", "degree": "", "thesis": "", "director": "", "student_name": ""}], "training": [{"hod": "", "score": "10", "nature": "Offline", "company": "Invitation for corporate training", "director": "", "duration": "1 DAy"}], "innovRows": [{"score": "2", "method": "Real-Time Industry Scenario-Based Learning", "details": "Designed classroom activities around real-world IT industry scenarios including server failures, cloud migration, scalability challenges, deployment automation, monitoring issues, and security practices to develop analytical and troubleshooting capabilities."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Outcome-Based and Skill-Focused Education", "details": "Focused on skill development through live demonstrations, mini-projects, use-case implementations, technical presentations, and continuous practical assessments aligned with industry expectations."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Industry Tool-Oriented Training Approach", "details": "Provided hands-on exposure to modern industry tools and platforms including Linux, Git, Jenkins, Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, SonarQube, Nexus, and AWS Cloud Services to enhance employability and industry readiness."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Learn by Doing Methodology", "details": "Implemented a “Theory + Practical Parallel Learning” approach where every concept taught in class is immediately demonstrated and practiced by students in the lab environment for better conceptual understanding and long-term retention."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Compulsory Hands-on Execution Model", "details": "Ensured mandatory student participation in practical implementation activities such as cloud deployment, Linux administration, CI/CD pipeline creation, Docker containerization, and infrastructure automation to promote experiential learning."}], "projects2": [{"hod": "", "role": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "sanction_date": "", "project_status": ""}], "proposals": [{"hod": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "director": "", "duration": ""}], "courseFile": [{"hod": "", "score": "10", "title": "BTech (CSE) CC Track - S