 Students were asked to design, simulate, and implement real-world applications using digital ICs to foster higher-order troubleshooting and design skills"}, {"score": "2", "method": "Video Case Study Method (Advanced Learners)", "details": "Operating System - BTech CSE SY Div. A + B: Students scoring 20 and more than 20 marks in the Midterm Exam were asked to write a case study on any one of the given topics and upload the self-videos explaining the same. Link (Div. A): https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1lxlHujVUiRFjIZg8Wtg64kNmWcNnCC-z?usp=drive_link. Link (Div. B): https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Uc_WdUxoLd8K-kuH5mzW7s10D2faousV?usp=drive_link"}, {"score": "2", "method": "Video-Based Learning (Slow Learners)", "details": "Operating System - BTech CSE SY Div. A + B: Students scoring less than 10 marks in the Midterm Exam were asked to upload the self-videos explaining answer of any one question and the numerical from the Midterm Question Paper. Link (Div. A): https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1UIYcM6yxfC3vypQtyPZEr7PA4iLcGT26?usp=drive_link. Link (Div. B): https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ciuUFM11e2c_CI0H0nk63ScmVeAshrLC?usp=drive_link"}, {"score": "2", "method": "Simulation-Based Learning (Advanced Learners)", "details": "Basic Electrical and Electronics Engineering - BTech CSE FY Div. I + J: Students scoring 20 and more than 20 marks in the Midterm Exam were asked to perform simulation on Tinkercad on any one of the given topics and submit the document consisting of the circuit diagram and results. Link (Div. I): https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1INNoOYr8hgihu7vAECICe3KI90t7MQkf?usp=drive_link. Link (Div. J): https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1GElvtBV4kUHq_HgXPsM45XjXbrbafy-T?usp=drive_link"}, {"score": "2", "method": "Video-Based Learning (Slow Learners)", "details": "Basic Electrical and Electronics Engineering - BTech CSE FY Div. I + J: Students scoring less than 10 marks in the Midterm Exam were asked to upload the self-videos explaining any three numerical from the Midterm Question Paper. Link (Div. I): https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1BZJwgbG8jVC6mk2I9aMkv0IRPokQvujX?usp=drive_link. Link (Div. J): https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1O7Mcq2KXnEuDjI_cNmqSo4BFZV5wf_Hw?usp=drive_link"}, {"score": "2", "method": "Blended Experiential Learning through Virtual Lab and NI ELVIS", "details": "Digital Logic Design Lab - BTech CSE FY Batch E3 + F1 + J1: The DLD Lab curriculum integrated cutting-edge pedagogical tools through Virtual Labs and NI ELVIS to enhance experiential learning. Virtual Labs provided students with self-paced, risk-free exploration of logic gates, minimizing component damage. Concurrently, the NI ELVIS platform bridged the gap between software simulation and physical hardware engineering."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Simulation-Based Inquiry Learning through Tinkercad", "details": "Basic Electrical and Electronics Engineering Lab - BTech CSE FY Batch J1 + J3: Students virtually constructed and debugged complex electronic circuits on Tinkercad"}, {"score": "2", "method": "Technology-Enabled Assessment through MCQ Quiz", "details": "Operating System - BTech CSE SY Div. A + B: To evaluate overall student learning and long-term knowledge retention, comprehensive MCQ Quizzes were conducted via JUNO covering the complete syllabus"}, {"score": "2", "method": "Technology-Enabled Assessment through MCQ Quiz", "details": "Basic Electrical and Electronics Engineering - BTech CSE FY Div. I + J: To evaluate overall student learning and long-term knowledge retention, a comprehensive MCQ Quiz was conducted via Google form covering the complete syllabus"}], "projects2": [{"hod": "", "role": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "sanction_date": "", "project_status": ""}], "proposals": [{"hod": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "director": "", "duration": ""}], "courseFile": [{"hod": "", "score": "20", "title": "CSE2104 - Operating Sy