 and its role in preventing microbial growth and enhancing shelf life. The activity helped students understand food preservation techniques through interactive and simulation-based learning."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Use of Learning Management System (LMS)", "details": "Utilized the Learning Management System (LMS) for sharing lecture notes, assignments, quizzes, and study materials with students in an organized manner. LMS was also used for continuous student interaction, attendance monitoring, and assessment activities."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Project Based Learning", "details": "Implemented project-based learning in Food Safety and Quality Control by assigning students to visit restaurants, mess facilities, and supermarkets for practical exposure to food hygiene and safety practices"}, {"score": "2", "method": "Open Course Ware (OCW) assignment", "details": "Assigned students to study resources related to Food Safety and Quality Control for additional subject understanding. Students completed assignments and submitted reports based on the concepts learned through these resources."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Quiz", "details": "Conducted online quizzes through the Learning Management System (LMS) as well as offline quizzes for various subjects to assess students' understanding of course concepts. The quiz activity promoted interactive learning and continuous evaluation of student performance."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Any Other Innovative Teaching-Learning", "details": "Assigned students a practical task to assess risks and opportunities related to food safety and quality management practices. Students analyzed the observations and prepared a detailed report to enhance their analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills."}], "projects2": [{"hod": "", "role": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "sanction_date": "", "project_status": ""}], "proposals": [{"hod": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "dire